        "markdown": "# Special Cards Database\n\nIn the classic game of **Illuminati**, **Special cards** are powerful, one-time-use action cards that bend the standard rules of play. They can cancel attacks, manipulate dice rolls, siphon funds, or alter alignments.\n\nBelow is the mechanical breakdown of all **15 classic Special cards** and our design proposals for adapting them into a modern digital card game layout.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Secrets Man Was Not Meant to Know\n*The ultimate cancel.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Can be played at any time to immediately cancel any other Special card as it is played. The cancelled Special card is discarded with no effect.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Cabal Silence*\n*   **Category**: **Instant Interrupt**\n*   **Effect**: Playable out-of-turn. Immediately negates and discards any special action card played by an opponent.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Assassination\n*Silent neutralization of an active asset.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Provides a +10 bonus to any attempt to destroy a group, or immediately neutralizes a group if played during an attack.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Liquidation*\n*   **Category**: **Removal Action**\n*   **Effect**: Instantly destroys an active non-Illuminati card on the board, bypasses standard defense checks, and sends it to the discard pile.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Bribery\n*Bypassing defenses with raw wealth.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Allows automatic control of any Corporate or Criminal group without rolling, or adds +10 to the control attempt.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Hostile Takeover*\n*   **Category**: **Capture Action**\n*   **Effect**: Allows the player to capture or take control of a target Corporate or Criminal card on the board without needing to meet normal capture conditions or roll.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Computer Espionage\n*Infiltrating information systems.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Allows a player to examine another player's hand of Special cards, or steal money from a target treasury.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Data Breach*\n*   **Category**: **Hand Disruption / Theft**\n*   **Effect**: View the opponent's entire hand of cards and discard one card of your choice, or siphon up to 5 resource points from their reserve pool.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Deep Agent\n*Double-cross and subversion.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Played to immediately take control of any action declared by another player, redirection of target, or canceling the action.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Subversion*\n*   **Category**: **Instant Redirect**\n*   **Effect**: Immediately intercept and redirect a target action declared by another player, choosing a new target of your choice.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Interference (2 Cards in Deck)\n*Disrupting coordination.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Can be played during any attack to add a +4 bonus to the defense or subtract -4 from the attack.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Jamming Signal*\n*   **Category**: **Defense Buff / Attack Debuff**\n*   **Effect**: Played during a conflict phase. Grants a defensive buff to an allied card or applies an attack penalty to an attacking opponent card.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Market Manipulation\n*Controlling the financial flow.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Doubles the income of all Corporate groups controlled by the player for one turn, or causes a crash.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Market Spike*\n*   **Category**: **Resource Multiplier**\n*   **Effect**: Doubles all resource income generated by your Corporate cards on the next turn, or forces an opponent's Corporate nodes to yield zero resource income.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Media Campaign\n*Shaping perception.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Adds +5 (or subtracts -5) to any control or neutralization attempt by manipulating media alignments.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Alignment Modulation*\n*   **Category**: **Utility Action**\n*   **Effect**: Temporarily changes or shifts the alignments of a target card on the board for the duration of the turn to gain compatibility bonuses.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Murphy's Law\n*If anything can go wrong, it will.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Forces a player to reroll any dice roll that was just made, or causes a declared action to automatically fail.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *System Glitch*\n*   **Category**: **Fail State Trigger**\n*   **Effect**: Playable when the opponent triggers a random or high-value card effect. Forces them to re-evaluate the outcome or outright cancels the action's execution.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Senate Investigating Committee\n*Official inquiries stalling operations.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Prevents one player from using any of their Special cards, or spending any Megabucks from their Illuminati treasury, for one full turn.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Audit Lock*\n*   **Category**: **Disrupt Action**\n*   **Effect**: Prevents a chosen opponent from playing special action cards or spending resources from their central treasury pool on their next turn.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Slush Fund\n*Hidden reserves.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Allows the player to draw 15 Megabucks immediately from the bank and place it in their Illuminati treasury.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Off-the-Books Cash*\n*   **Category**: **Resource Injection**\n*   **Effect**: Instantly adds a massive burst of resource points to the player's central pool. This card is exiled from the game after one use.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Swiss Bank Account\n*Fortified wealth.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Allows a player to move up to 10 Megabucks to a secure \"Swiss Bank Account\" where it cannot be stolen or targeted by any Special cards.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Secured Vault*\n*   **Category**: **Resource Shield**\n*   **Effect**: Shields a portion of your resources, rendering them immune to siphoning, theft, or target actions by opponent cards.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Whispering Campaign\n*Subversive rumors.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Changes the alignment of any one group card for one turn, or lowers its resistance by 4.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Smear Campaign*\n*   **Category**: **Defense Debuff**\n*   **Effect**: Decreases the defense or resistance value of a target card by 4 for the duration of the turn.\n\n---\n\n## 14. White Collar Crime\n*Embezzlement and financial schemes.*\n\n### Classic Effect\n*   Immediately steals 5 Megabucks from any other player's treasury and transfers it to your own.\n\n### Modern Adaptation Concept\n*   **Action Name**: *Embezzle*\n*   **Category**: **Theft Action**\n*   **Effect**: Instantly transfers a set amount of resource points from the target opponent's treasury directly to the player's treasury."
